  <div class="page-wrapper">
 
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <span class="hero-tag">03 / Business Profile</span>
        <h1>GoNoodle:<br /><em>Where Movement Meets Wellbeing</em></h1>
        <p>
          A high-performing industry leader that has bridged the gap between physical activity
          and mental regulation for over 40 million children — and what it means for the
          future of SEL.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>
 
    <main class="container">
 
      <!-- OVERVIEW -->
      <div class="profile-banner fade-in">
        <div class="profile-left">
          <div class="gonoodle-logo">
            <div class="gn-circle">G</div>
            <span>oNoodle</span>
          </div>
          <p class="profile-tagline">
            Bridging the gap between physical activity and mental regulation
            for over 40 million children in K–5 classrooms across the country.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="profile-metrics stagger-parent">
          <div class="pm-item">
            <span class="pm-val">40M+</span>
            <span class="pm-lbl">Children Reached</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pm-item">
            <span class="pm-val">K–5</span>
            <span class="pm-lbl">Target Grade Range</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pm-item">
            <span class="pm-val">Free</span>
            <span class="pm-lbl">Core Platform Access</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pm-item">
            <span class="pm-val">3–5</span>
            <span class="pm-lbl">Min. Activity Breaks</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
 
      <!-- BUSINESS MODEL -->
      <div class="subsection-title fade-in"><h3>Business Model &amp; Key Features</h3></div>
 
      <div class="features-grid stagger-parent fade-in">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="fc-icon">🏫</div>
          <h4>Classroom-First Design</h4>
          <p>GoNoodle is built for instant classroom deployment — 3–5 minute movement breaks that teachers can play immediately with zero prep. Designed to fit within the natural rhythm of a school day.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="fc-icon">🏠</div>
          <h4>Classroom-to-Home Connectivity</h4>
          <p>A distinctive innovation: GoNoodle extends into the home, enabling parents to engage with the same content their children use in school. This continuity amplifies SEL impact beyond the classroom walls.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="fc-icon">🎮</div>
          <h4>Gamified Engagement</h4>
          <p>Classes earn points, level up their characters, and unlock new content — creating intrinsic motivation for movement and emotional regulation activities rather than treating them as obligations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="fc-icon">🌍</div>
          <h4>Democratized Access</h4>
          <p>The free core platform ensures that access to mental health support tools is not gated by district budget. This equity-first approach aligns with GoNoodle's mission to reach all children regardless of background.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
 
      <!-- SWOT -->
      <div class="subsection-title fade-in"><h3>SWOT Analysis</h3></div>
 
      <div class="swot-grid stagger-parent">
        <div class="swot-card swot-s">
          <div class="swot-badge">Strengths</div>
          <ul class="swot-list">
            <li>Unique intersection of movement + SEL, scientifically validated by 2024 meta-analysis</li>
            <li>Classroom-to-home connectivity bridges school and family engagement</li>
            <li>Free access democratizes mental health support across income levels</li>
            <li>Gamified, age-appropriate content drives high engagement among K–5</li>
            <li>Established trust and recognition with 40M+ users</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="swot-card swot-w">
          <div class="swot-badge">Weaknesses</div>
          <ul class="swot-list">
            <li>Limited data analytics capabilities compared to competitors like Panorama</li>
            <li>Primarily K–5 focus limits market reach and long-term user retention</li>
            <li>Revenue model partially reliant on advertising in free tier</li>
            <li>Lower brand awareness among parents relative to teachers</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="swot-card swot-o">
          <div class="swot-badge">Opportunities</div>
          <ul class="swot-list">
            <li>Growing Wellbeing-as-a-Service market — $21B projected by 2033</li>
            <li>AI integration for personalized movement and SEL programming</li>
            <li>Expansion into middle school (grades 6–8) content library</li>
            <li>Federal funding streams via ESSA and American Rescue Plan Act</li>
            <li>International market expansion beyond US classrooms</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="swot-card swot-t">
          <div class="swot-badge">Threats</div>
          <ul class="swot-list">
            <li>Political attacks on SEL in some states limiting school adoption</li>
            <li>Well-funded competitors (Panorama Education, ClassDojo, Second Step)</li>
            <li>Teacher burnout limiting consistent SEL implementation</li>
            <li>Data privacy regulations in K-12 creating compliance burden</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
 
      <!-- COMPETITORS -->
      <div class="subsection-title fade-in"><h3>Competitive Landscape</h3></div>
 
      <div class="competitor-wrap fade-in">
        <table class="comp-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Company</th>
              <th>Primary Focus</th>
              <th>Key Differentiator</th>
              <th>Grade Range</th>
              <th>Price Model</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="row-hl">
              <td><strong>GoNoodle ★</strong></td>
              <td>Movement + Mental Regulation</td>
              <td>Physical activity as SEL driver</td>
              <td>K–5</td>
              <td>Freemium</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Panorama Education</td>
              <td>SEL Analytics &amp; Assessment</td>
              <td>Data dashboards, 42% accuracy improvement</td>
              <td>K–12</td>
              <td>Paid (district)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>ClassDojo</td>
              <td>Classroom Culture &amp; Communication</td>
              <td>Parent-teacher-student connection</td>
              <td>K–8</td>
              <td>Free + Premium</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Nearpod SEL</td>
              <td>Interactive SEL Lessons</td>
              <td>Embedded in curriculum delivery</td>
              <td>K–12</td>
              <td>Freemium</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Second Step</td>
              <td>Evidence-Based SEL Curriculum</td>
              <td>Long-form, research-backed lessons</td>
              <td>PreK–8</td>
              <td>Paid (school)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
 
      <!-- ACTIVITY + SEL -->
      <div class="subsection-title fade-in"><h3>The Science: Activity &amp; SEL</h3></div>
 
      <div class="science-section fade-in">
        <p class="lead-text">
          GoNoodle's most powerful differentiator is the scientific validation of its core
          model. The 2024 meta-analysis of 32 studies confirmed that physical activity
          interventions consistently improve SEL outcomes in elementary school children.
        </p>
        <p>
          Movement activates the body's stress-response systems, improves self-regulation,
          and creates positive social experiences through cooperative activity. GoNoodle
          translates this research into classroom-ready, 3–5 minute breaks that teachers
          can deploy instantly — no training, no setup, no cost.
        </p>
 
        <div class="science-diagram stagger-parent">
          <div class="sd-node sd-center">
            <span>Physical<br />Movement</span>
          </div>
          <div class="sd-arrow">→</div>
          <div class="sd-outcomes">
            <div class="sd-outcome">Self-Regulation</div>
            <div class="sd-outcome">Social Awareness</div>
            <div class="sd-outcome">Emotional Health</div>
            <div class="sd-outcome">Academic Readiness</div>
          </div>
        </div>
 
        <div class="research-cite">
          <strong>Source:</strong> Moon et al. (2024). <em>Review of Education</em>, Wiley — Meta-analysis of 32 physical activity intervention studies in elementary school children. First meta-analysis of its kind to examine physical activity's effect specifically on SEL outcomes.
        </div>
      </div>
 
